From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 19:17:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] iio: proximity: vl53l0x-i2c: identify the sensor after
 powering it on

Probe reads the model ID register before it enables the vdd supply and
releases the XSHUT reset line, so it only works on boards where the sensor
happens to be powered and out of shutdown already. On the Pixel 2 XL the
supply is off and XSHUT is held low at boot, the read fails, and probe
returns -EINVAL.

Read the ID once vl53l0x_power_on() has run, and report the error it
actually got. With that the sensor probes and ranges (about 150 mm to a
book in front of the rear camera).

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/iio/proximity/vl53l0x-i2c.c | 16 +++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iio/proximity/vl53l0x-i2c.c b/drivers/iio/proximity/vl53l0x-i2c.c
index b7127c3c52d2..64275009d7fb 100644
--- a/drivers/iio/proximity/vl53l0x-i2c.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/proximity/vl53l0x-i2c.c
@@ -325,13 +325,6 @@ static int vl53l0x_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 				     I2C_FUNC_SMBUS_BYTE_DATA))
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 
-	ret = i2c_smbus_read_byte_data(data->client, VL_REG_IDENTIFICATION_MODEL_ID);
-	if (ret < 0)
-		return -EINVAL;
-
-	if (ret != VL53L0X_MODEL_ID_VAL)
-		dev_info(&client->dev, "Unknown model id: 0x%x", ret);
-
 	data->vdd_supply = devm_regulator_get(&client->dev, "vdd");
 	if (IS_ERR(data->vdd_supply))
 		return dev_err_probe(&client->dev, PTR_ERR(data->vdd_supply),
@@ -351,6 +344,15 @@ static int vl53l0x_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/* only a powered sensor out of shutdown answers on the bus */
+	ret = i2c_smbus_read_byte_data(data->client, VL_REG_IDENTIFICATION_MODEL_ID);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		return dev_err_probe(&client->dev, ret,
+				     "Failed to read the model ID\n");
+
+	if (ret != VL53L0X_MODEL_ID_VAL)
+		dev_info(&client->dev, "Unknown model id: 0x%x", ret);
+
 	indio_dev->name = "vl53l0x";
 	indio_dev->info = &vl53l0x_info;
 	indio_dev->channels = vl53l0x_channels;
